## Model card and raw evidence

Six fresh broad and exact-name searches covering official identity, benchmarks and API/pricing did not establish an OMI Alpha language model. Exact hyphenated model/API queries returned no results; the spaced exact name mostly identifies a historical cipher machine. Broad searches found the Omi wearable, Open Model Initiative and the differently named Omen Alpha. None supplies a publisher mapping to `omi-alpha`.

The [live Zen catalog](https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/models), retrieved October 27, has no `omi-alpha` route. Local metadata's September 2026 release, 1,048,576 context, 256,000 output, image input and $0.40/$3.20 pricing assertions could not be traced to a public primary source. They remain unverified; no guessed OMI API hostname is treated as documentation.

Publisher, architecture, parameters, cutoff, modalities and access terms remain unresolved. No verified public exact-model reasoning, tool, coding, vision or retrieval scores found. Omen Alpha, Omni Alpha and Omi's speech products are not silently substituted for this identity.

